Subject: [PATCH] iio: qcom_smgr: direct reads of the latest sample

The Sensor Manager only streams samples, so the accelerometer offered a
buffer and no raw channels. iio-sensor-proxy cannot use that buffer: it has
no trigger, and the proxy's buffer driver needs one. Its polling driver
reads in_accel_{x,y,z}_raw instead.

Keep the latest sample of every report, and add smgr_sensor_read(): when
no stream runs, it requests one at up to 10 Hz (or the lower sampling
frequency) and waits for its first sample; later reads return the latest
sample at once. The stream stops 3 s after the last read. A buffer enable
replaces the polling stream, and a buffer disable ends any stream, so the
two cannot leave a report running behind each other. Give the
accelerometer's x, y and z channels a raw value that reads in direct mode.

Also skip reports without samples and the buffer push while no IIO device
is bound.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5

--- a/drivers/iio/accel/smgr_accel.c
